			<div class="content" id="post-content-4768821">
									

<p>I’m prefacing this by stating that I haven't heard of the Anishnaabe peoples and their cultural traditions and legends.</p>
<p>The hook of your containment procedures and image are very nice, and the inclusion of a nexus zone is always something I enjoy reading. As I stated already, I didn’t know about these myths and was ready for this to be a standard horror setup where this tribe is setting up the Foundation to die to please these creatures. I can’t tell you how happy I was <em>not</em> to have that be the outcome.</p>
<p>Somehow this had an odd hit of realism to it, more than I find with most SCPs, I’m not sure if it’s your writing style (which, may I say, is great) or the subject matter but this was an enthralling read all the way through.</p>
<p>My only real criticism is that I feel like this could be cut down very slightly, as the pretty consistent pacing faltered for me around the last two or so test logs. This wasn’t enough to sway my vote, and I love a good folklore/legend based SCP. Easy +1.</p>

							</div>

								
					
